VALUES ('55b8b367-19e6-4d2f-b8b7-ae399aca4c99', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000400', 'Despite these developments, President Meles pledged to oversee the formation of multiparty democracy. In June 1994, there were elections for a 547-member Constituent Assembly that adopted the constitution of the Federal Democratic Republic of Ethiopia. Moreover, the Transitional Charter also established 14 “self-governing regions” of “nations, nationalities, and peoples". Thus from 1991 to 1995, Ethiopia was gradually evolving into a federal system of government. 1.What were the major problems of the Transitional Period, and how were they solved? 2.Identify major political parties that participated in the conference drafting of the 1991 Transitional Charter. ', 'G10-History-STB-2023-web.pdf p.1', '2026.1', 'published', '[-0.0110875815,0.004918126,0.0375561,-0.02101126,0.026473748,-0.013581402,-0.016206075,-0.024486082,0.03854085,-0.0993182,-0.045047045,-0.0005378795,0.040674407,-0.0133188525,-0.03455846,-0.049218595,0.017825011,-0.00666037,0.0074930275,-0.01009894,0.027042463,0.034698926,0.011343341,-0.030672435,-0.031309612,0.009069703,-0.009381521,-0.025565222,-0.01869417,0.18850984,-0.062033314,-0.02503817,0.017137436,-0.029796796,0.013785364,-0.0398525,-0.008371361,-0.008115038,0.026252842,0.006025074,0.027593896,0.00974499,0.023619393,0.031655997,-0.026274338,-0.010586915,-0.05347877,0.010675934,-0.008276459,0.05256951,0.016846033,-0.02793766,0.025766626,-0.05561409,0.016477637,0.033760764,0.0040043355,0.020376546,0.053908132,0.011196926,0.0120207835,0.035048116,0.002405011,0.0033251196,-0.020762173,-0.017774142,0.013723259,-0.043117274,0.012537359,-0.0041140313,-0.021418838,0.008695527,0.035128605,0.008001493,-0.024584047,0.0018202902,-0.052831512,0.02804582,0.016113043,0.04363461,0.015286736,0.029021652,0.00047932184,0.018495169,0.03986877,0.033026878,0.012861891,-0.025434272,-0.008746465,-0.014615195,0.002661048,0.03098801,0.019868461,-0.040470745,-0.007947508,0.0230885